
# Workspace Context — BraTS / MR-RATE Diffusion Model Project
Last updated: 2026-04-03

---

## What We're Building

A **2D slice-based diffusion model** (DDPM/DDIM) with **learned variance (VLB loss)**,
trained exclusively on healthy thin-slice T1w brain MRI from the MR-RATE dataset.
**Goal:** Unsupervised anomaly detection — given a diseased slice, reconstruct the healthy
version and expose pathology via the residual `|x₀ − x̂₀|` and the model's uncertainty map.

---

## Anomaly Detection Pipeline (inference)

```
BraTS T1 slice  x₀
      │
      ▼
Binary mask M  (GT seg or ACAT saliency)
      │
      ▼
DDIM encode  →  x_L
      (forward noising applied only inside mask M, to noise level L)
      │
      ▼
Hybrid DDPM + DDIM decode  (t = L → 0)
      ├─ inside  M = 1  →  DDPM steps  (stochastic, free to regenerate healthy anatomy)
      └─ outside M = 0  →  DDIM steps  (deterministic, preserves healthy anatomy exactly)
      │
      ├─ captures uncertainty = exp(log_var) at t=L  (from learned variance head)
      ▼
Healthy reconstruction  x̂₀
      │
      ▼
Recon anomaly  = | x₀ − x̂₀ |          (smoothed, σ=2 px)
Uncertainty    = exp(log σ²) @ t=L     (model confidence map)
Combined score = recon_anomaly × uncertainty
```

**Key inference hyperparameters:**
- `ENCODE_T` — how far to noise (250 / 500 / 750): higher = more freedom to edit pathology
- `N_DDIM_STEPS` — reverse decode steps (50 is standard)
- `smooth_sigma` — Gaussian smoothing on anomaly map (default 2.0 px)

