## Dataset

### Healthy Brain Data — `brain_only/`
- **Source:** Hugging Face Hub `hf://buckets/rahul2001/mr-rate-processed`
- **Downloaded via:** `load_mr_rate_data.ipynb` (421 files synced)
- **Total folders:** 212 subjects (alphanumeric IDs, e.g. `4IJW45J4TC`)
- Each folder contains: `t1_brain.nii.gz`, optionally `t2_axi_brain.nii.gz`,
  `flair_brain.nii.gz`, `t2_cor_brain.nii.gz`, `brain_mask.nii.gz`

### BraTS 2020 — `BraTS2020_TrainingData/`
- 371 glioma cases, each with `_flair.nii`, `_t1.nii`, `_t1ce.nii`, `_t2.nii`, `_seg.nii`
- Volume shape: (240, 240, 155), 1 mm isotropic
- Seg labels: 0=background, 1=necrotic/non-enhancing, 2=edema, 3=enhancing tumor
- **Role:** evaluation / reference only — not in training pipeline

---

## Key Dataset Decision: Thin-Slice Only

After analysing all 210 subjects we found two fundamentally different acquisition types:

| Group | Subjects | Z-spacing | Depth range | Slices/subj (after filter) |
|-------|----------|-----------|-------------|---------------------------|
| **Thick (excluded)** | 139 | 4–7 mm | 20–30 | 14–25 |
| **Thin (used)** | 71 | 0.47–1.04 mm | 200–640 | 73–315 |

**Thin-slice split (deterministic, seed=42, 80/10/10):**

| Split | Subjects | Usable 2D slices |
|-------|----------|-----------------|
| Train | 55 | 9,540 |
| Val | 7 | 1,125 |
| Test | 9 | 1,995 |
| **Total** | **71** | **12,660** |

**Fill rate stats (thin-slice, 15–85% Z window):**
- 17,594 candidate slices before fill filter
- **28% dropped** by the 5% fill filter → 12,660 retained

---

## Slice Statistics (raw → usable)

```
All 210 subjects — raw axial slices         :  28,412  (100%)
  After 15%–85% Z-range filter              :  20,074  (−29.3%)
  After 5% brain-fill filter                :  15,119  (−24.7% of candidates)

Thin-slice only (71 subjects):
  Candidate slices in 15%–85% window         :  17,594
  After 5% fill filter                      :  12,660  (72.0% retained)
```

